@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il05-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il05-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-k`
IMPORT `nii-s348-maximum-minimum`

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], s 342 (החייבים בתשלום דמי ביטוח) — who is liable to pay
-- insurance contributions, and the employer's deduction from the wage. Quotations (`src:N`) are copied
-- mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHICH YEARS (NOTES.md, assumption A1). s 342's last tag, תשפ״ה־7, counts to the Law for the 2025
-- budget year. Its s 19(4) replaced "60% of the average wage" with "the reduced collection threshold"
-- throughout s 342, and its s 21 commences that chapter on 1 January 2026 (fetched from the Knesset
-- 2026-10-06; NOTES.md section 7). So the deposited text is the text from 1 January 2026, and this
-- module answers months from January 2026; before that, (e)(3) and (f) spoke of 60% of the average
-- wage, which is not encoded.
--
-- WHAT IS DUTY AND WHAT IS ARITHMETIC. (a) and (b) make persons liable, (c) obliges the employer to
-- deduct and forbids it in some months, (d) makes the employee pay or be refunded. Each has a party
-- and an act, but what follows from not paying or not deducting is in other sections (the collection
-- and interest provisions), none of them in this row, so nothing here would be produced by a breach.
-- They are encoded as who is liable and how much (phrasebook entry 5.2), not as obligations.

§ `Section 342 — who is liable to pay insurance contributions`
-- src:3658 | סעיף 342 – החייבים בתשלום דמי ביטוח [תיקון: תשנ״ז, תשנ״ח, תש״ס־2, תשס״ד, תשס״ה־6, תשע״ז־5, תשע״ז־12, תשפ״ה־7]

§§ `342(a)-(b) — the insured person for himself, the employer for the employee`

-- src:3659 | (א) מבוטח שהוא עובד עצמאי, ומבוטח שאינו עובד ואינו עובד עצמאי, חייבים בתשלום דמי ביטוח בעד עצמם; ואולם מבוטחת לפי פרק ג׳ בלבד מכוח היותה אשת מבוטח אינה חייבת בתשלום דמי הביטוח.
-- src:3660 | (ב) המעביד חייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח בעד עובדו; היה המבוטח עובד אצל מעבידים שונים ישלם כל אחד מהם את דמי הביטוח כאילו הוא בלבד היה מעבידו, ועל המבוטח יחולו הוראות סעיפים קטנים (ד) ו־(ה).
-- (a) "An insured person who is self-employed, and an insured person who is neither employee nor
-- self-employed, are liable to pay contributions for themselves; but an insured woman under Chapter C
-- only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person, is not liable to pay the contributions."
-- (b) "The employer is liable to pay contributions for his employee; if the insured person works for
-- different employers, each of them pays the contributions as if he alone were his employer, and
-- subsections (d) and (e) apply to the insured person." (b)'s "as if he alone" is how each employer's
-- deduction under (c) is computed: on the wage it pays. The exception in (a) is to (a)'s sentence,
-- about those who pay for themselves.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(a)-(b) (source lines 3659-3660)
GIVEN p IS AN `An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)`
GIVETH A `The person liable to pay the contributions under section 342`
`s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `column`
    WHEN `an employee` THEN `the employer, for the employee`
    OTHERWISE
        IF   p's `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person`
        THEN `no one: an insured woman under Chapter C only, as the wife of an insured person, is not liable`
        ELSE `the insured person, for himself`

-- Version 0.4.0 (05-P3; the independent tester's A7; the Axiom comparison's X5). One who is both an
-- employee and self-employed (s 342(f), "עובד שהוא גם עובד עצמאי", source line 3673) is reached by
-- (b) as an employee and by (a) as self-employed: the employer pays for him, and he pays for
-- himself. Each status he has is put to the rule above, so one call answers as the two calls did.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(a)-(b) (source lines 3659-3660); s 342(f) (source line 3673)
GIVEN p IS AN `An insured person who may be both an employee and self-employed, for section 342(a)-(b)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `The person liable to pay the contributions under section 342`
`s 342(a)-(b) — the persons liable to pay the contributions for` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF p's `works as an employee` AND p's `works as a self-employed person` THEN LIST (`as` `an employee`), (`as` `a self-employed person`)
           IF p's `works as an employee`                                         THEN LIST (`as` `an employee`)
           IF p's `works as a self-employed person`                              THEN LIST (`as` `a self-employed person`)
           OTHERWISE                                                                  LIST (`as` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`)
    WHERE
        `as` c MEANS
            `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for`
                (`An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH
                    `column`                                                                          IS c
                    `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS p's `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person`)

§§ `342(c)(1) — the employer deducts the employee's share from the wage`

-- src:3661 | (ג)(1) היו דמי ביטוח משתלמים בעד עובד לפי סעיף 335(א), (ד), (ה), (ז), (ח) או (ט), ינכה המעביד משכרו של העובד אחוזים מההכנסה שלפיה משתלמים דמי הביטוח כאמור בלוח י׳ ובסעיף 337.
-- "If contributions are payable for an employee under s 335(a), (d), (e), (g), (h) or (i), the employer
-- shall deduct from the employee's wage percentages of the income on which the contributions are
-- payable, as stated in Schedule J and in s 337." s 335 imposes contributions branch by branch:
-- src:3611 | (א) עובד או עובד עצמאי שאינו תושב ישראל ישתלמו בעדו דמי ביטוח אימהות.
-- src:3614 | (ד) מבוטח לפי פרק ו׳ ישולמו בעדו דמי ביטוח נפגעי תאונות.
-- src:3615 | (ה) מבוטח לפי פסקה (1) להגדרת [note: ”]מבוטח[note: “] שבסעיף 158 למעט בעל שליטה בחברת מעטים ישתלמו בעדו דמי ביטוח אבטלה.
-- src:3617 | (ז) מבוטח לפי פרק ט׳ ישתלמו בעדו דמי ביטוח נכות.
-- src:3618 | (ח) מבוטח ביטוח סיעוד ישתלמו בעדו דמי ביטוח סיעוד.
-- src:3619 | (ט) מבוטח לפי פרק י״א למעט עקרת בית ואלמנה בת קצבה כהגדרתן בסעיף 238 ישתלמו בעדו דמי ביטוח אזרחים ותיקים ושאירים ודמי ביטוח אימהות, בין שהוא מבוטח גם לפי פרק ג׳ ובין שאינו מבוטח לפיו.
-- so the six subsections are the branches maternity ((a), and (i)), accident injury ((d)),
-- unemployment ((e)), disability ((g)), long-term care ((h)) and senior citizens and survivors ((i));
-- not children ((b)), work injury ((c)) or insolvency ((f)) (fork F12). Schedule J's column D, "the
-- deduction from the employee's wage for s 342(c)", prints a figure for exactly those six (row IL-04's
-- tests check this).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661); s 335 (source lines 3611-3619)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`the branches of the subsections of section 335 that section 342(c)(1) names` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661)
GIVEN m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`s 342(c)(1) — the branches in which the employer deducts, for` m MEANS
    filter `named by section 342(c)(1)` (m's `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`)
    WHERE
        `named by section 342(c)(1)` b MEANS elem b `the branches of the subsections of section 335 that section 342(c)(1) names`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661); Schedule J column D (row IL-04)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the case gives no column D amount for a branch in which the employer deducts` MEANS
    REFUSE "the case gives no column D amount for a branch in which the employer deducts"

-- The column D amount the case gives for a branch (one entry per branch, input convention).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661); Schedule J column D (source lines 4716-4729, 4734-4747; row IL-04)
GIVEN b IS A `A branch of insurance`
      m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column D amount for` b `, in` m MEANS
    CONSIDER filter `for this branch` (m's `the column D amounts on the wage`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the case gives no column D amount for a branch in which the employer deducts`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x's `amount`
    WHERE
        `for this branch` x MEANS x's `branch` EQUALS b

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661)
GIVEN m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `the column D amount for` b `, in` m) (`s 342(c)(1) — the branches in which the employer deducts, for` m))

§§ `342(c)(2) — no deduction while a senior citizen pension is payable, or after the age`

-- src:3662 | (2) המעביד לא ינכה משכר עובדו את האחוזים האמורים בעד הזמן שבעדו מגיעה למבוטח קצבת אזרח ותיק ובעד הזמן שלאחר הגיע המבוטח לגיל 70 שנים בגבר, ובאשה – לגיל הקבוע לגביה, בהתאם לחודש לידתה, בחלק ד׳ בלוח א׳1, בכפוף להוראות סעיף 245(ב2), אף אם לא מגיעה למבוטח קצבת אזרח ותיק, ואם העובד הוא שוטר כמשמעותו בחוק המשטרה או סוהר כמשמעותו בחוק שירות בתי הסוהר, לא ינוכה משכרם הניכוי כאמור בפרט 6 ללוח י׳; ואולם המעביד רשאי להפחית מדמי הביטוח שהוא חייב בהם את הסכומים שהיה מנכה משכרו של העובד אילולא הוראה זו בחוק; בפסקה זו, ”קצבת אזרח ותיק“ – לרבות גמלת אזרח ותיק מיוחדת.
-- "The employer shall not deduct those percentages from his employee's wage for the time for which a
-- senior citizen pension is payable to the insured, and for the time after the insured reaches 70 for
-- a man, and for a woman the age fixed for her, by her month of birth, in Part D of Schedule A1,
-- subject to s 245(b2), even if no senior citizen pension is payable to the insured; and if the
-- employee is a police officer under the Police Law or a prison officer under the Prison Service Law,
-- the deduction in item 6 of Schedule J shall not be deducted from their wage; but the employer may
-- reduce from the contributions he is liable for the amounts he would have deducted from the
-- employee's wage but for this provision; in this paragraph, 'senior citizen pension' includes a
-- special senior citizen benefit."
-- "subject to s 245(b2)": s 245(b2) reads "(בוטל)", repealed (source line 2474), so there is nothing to
-- be subject to (fork F10; nii-il05-tests-expected-red.l4).
-- Item 6 of Schedule J is unemployment (source line 4725; fork F21).
-- "the time after": a month is wholly that time if the insured reached the age on or before its first
-- day. A month in which the age is reached later, or for part of which the pension is payable, is
-- split by the text into time with and time without a deduction, and the text does not say how a
-- monthly wage is split: declined (fork F9).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662)
GIVEN p IS A `The insured person, for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c)(2) — the age, in months, after which no deduction is made, for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a man` THEN 70 TIMES 12
    WHEN `a woman` `the age in months` THEN `the age in months`

-- The day the insured reaches that age: the date of birth moved on by that many months. `add months`
-- keeps the day of the month, or the month's last day if it is shorter (31 January plus one month is
-- 28 or 29 February; fork F19).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662)
GIVEN m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 342(c)(2) — the day the insured reaches the age, for` m MEANS
    `add months` (m's `date of birth`) (`s 342(c)(2) — the age, in months, after which no deduction is made, for` (m's `the insured person`))

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the insured reaches the age during it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the insured reaches the age during it"

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the senior citizen pension is payable for part of it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the senior citizen pension is payable for part of it"

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662)
GIVEN m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 342(c)(2) — no deduction is made for the month, for` m MEANS
    BRANCH IF Day `the day the age is reached` AT MOST Day `the first day of the month`          THEN TRUE
           IF m's `senior citizen pension` EQUALS `payable for the whole month`                    THEN TRUE
           IF m's `senior citizen pension` EQUALS `payable for part of the month`                  THEN `section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the senior citizen pension is payable for part of it`
           IF Day `the day the age is reached` GREATER THAN Day `the last day of the month`        THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `section 342(c)(2) does not say how a month's deduction is divided when the insured reaches the age during it`
    WHERE
        `the day the age is reached` MEANS `s 342(c)(2) — the day the insured reaches the age, for` m
        `the first day of the month` MEANS YMD (m's `tax year`) (m's `month`) 1
        `the last day of the month`  MEANS YMD (m's `tax year`) (m's `month`) (`Days in month` (m's `month`) (m's `tax year`))

§§ `342(c) — what the employer deducts`

-- src:3666 | (ה) השר רשאי לקבוע תנאים, כללים ומועדים בדבר –
-- src:3667 | (1) חובת עובד לדווח למעבידו ולמוסד על היותו עובד אצל מעביד נוסף;
-- src:3668 | (2) תשלום או החזר של ההפרש שבין סכום הניכוי בפועל, לבין סכום דמי הביטוח המתואמים;
-- src:3669 | (3) חובת מעביד לנכות דמי ביטוח בשיעור החל, לפי טור ה׳ בלוח י׳, על הכנסת עובד העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת, גם מהכנסת העובד שאינה עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת, אם העובד מועסק אצל מעביד נוסף;
-- src:3670 | (4) אישור המוסד בדבר ניכוי דמי ביטוח בשיעורים הנקובים בטור ה׳ בלוח י׳, לפי הענין, בשונה מההוראות שנקבעו לפי פסקה (3), וכן בדבר חובת מעביד לנכות מהכנסת עובד המועסק על ידי מעבידים שונים, דמי ביטוח בהתאם לאישור המוסד.
-- src:3671 | [note: פורסמו תקנות הביטוח הלאומי (תשלום וניכוי דמי ביטוח משכר מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים), התשנ״ז–1997.]
-- (e)(3)-(4) let the Minister require an employer of an employee who has another employer to deduct
-- at the full rate on the whole wage, and let the Institute approve other rates; regulations were made
-- (5757-1997, noted at source line 3671) and are not in the sources. Where they govern a deduction,
-- (c) alone does not give it: declined.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(3)-(4) (source lines 3669-3670); the regulations of 5757-1997 (source line 3671)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the deduction is governed by regulations under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4), which are not encoded here` MEANS
    REFUSE "the deduction is governed by regulations under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4), which are not encoded here"

§§ `Version 0.3.0: Schedule J's totals row or its items (row IL-04's fork F4)`

-- (c)(1) deducts "percentages ... as in Schedule J". Where Schedule J's totals row and its items
-- differ (column D's upper part: 7.00 printed, 4.67 by the items, row IL-04 section 0), row IL-04's
-- fork F4 was ruled by Meng on 2026-10-07: the printed totals govern by default, the items' reading
-- kept as the alternative. Schedule J is row IL-04's; this row takes its column D figures as inputs.
-- At the items' reading the (c)(1) deduction is the sum of the per-branch amounts the case gives (as
-- in versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0). At the printed totals it is one amount for the branches in which the
-- employer deducts together, which no per-branch list can carry: it is an argument, `the column D
-- amount at the printed totals`, row IL-04's `the column D deduction under` at its default reading
-- for those branches (`s 342(c)(1) — the branches in which the employer deducts, for`). The rules
-- whose names do not mention the reading keep their 0.1.0 names and read the items, so that callers
-- built before 0.3.0 still answer as they did; the rules "at the printed totals" follow the switch.
@ref row IL-04's fork F4 (Schedule J totals rows, source lines 4730, 4748); Meng's ruling of 2026-10-07
GIVETH A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
`section 342(c) — the reading of Schedule J this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` MEANS
    `the printed totals govern`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661); Schedule J column D (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN m              IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the items govern`          THEN `s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m
    WHEN `the printed totals govern` THEN `at the totals`

-- The deduction (c) requires for a month, after (c)(2). Each employer of an employee with several
-- employers computes it on the wage it pays, "as if he alone were his employer" ((b)). A police or
-- prison officer: "the deduction in item 6 of Schedule J" is left out, at either reading the item's
-- own amount (at the printed totals: the total less item 6's amount; fork F23).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1)-(2) (source lines 3661-3662); s 342(b) (source line 3660); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN m              IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    BRANCH IF m's `tax year` LESS THAN 2026
              THEN `this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only`
           IF m's `month` LESS THAN 1 OR m's `month` GREATER THAN 12
              THEN `a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12`
           IF m's `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)`
              THEN `the deduction is governed by regulations under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4), which are not encoded here`
           IF `s 342(c)(2) — no deduction is made for the month, for` m
              THEN 0
           IF m's `a police officer or a prison officer`
              THEN `s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MINUS `the item 6 deduction`
           OTHERWISE `s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`
    WHERE
        `the item 6 deduction` MEANS
            IF   elem `unemployment` (`s 342(c)(1) — the branches in which the employer deducts, for` m)
            THEN `the column D amount for` `unemployment` `, in` m
            ELSE 0

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0, by its old name: the items' reading (the argument for the
-- printed totals is not read at that reading).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1)-(2) (source lines 3661-3662); the items' reading of Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`  @desc the month, whose column D amounts must be on the wage as section 348(a) takes it into account; on a wage above the Schedule K maximum, `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` applies the maximum itself (05-RC2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m MEANS
    `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0

-- At the reading the switch names (the printed totals).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1)-(2) (source lines 3661-3662); the switch above
GIVEN m              IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` `section 342(c) — the reading of Schedule J this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

-- "the employer may reduce from the contributions he is liable for the amounts he would have deducted
-- from the employee's wage but for this provision": the deduction (c)(1) requires, less the one made.
-- A permission: the employer need not use it.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2), last limb (source line 3662)
GIVEN m IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c)(2) — the amount by which the employer may reduce the contributions he is liable for, for` m MEANS
    `s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m MINUS `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2), last limb (source line 3662); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN m              IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c)(2) — the amount by which the employer may reduce the contributions he is liable for, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(c)(1) — the deduction it requires, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MINUS `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` m `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

§§ `342(d) — an employee with several employers`

-- src:3663 | (ד) היה המבוטח עובד אצל מעבידים שונים, יחולו לגביו הוראות אלה:
-- src:3664 | (1) היה הסכום שנוכה מהכנסתו החודשית הכוללת של המבוטח מכל מעבידיו (בסעיף זה – הניכוי בפועל), נמוך מהסכום שהיה על כל מעבידיו לנכות מהכנסתו החודשית הכוללת, אילו שולמה לו על ידי מעביד אחד (בסעיף זה – דמי ביטוח מתואמים), יהיה העובד חייב בתשלום ההפרש שבין הניכוי בפועל לבין דמי הביטוח המתואמים;
-- src:3665 | (2) היה סכום הניכוי בפועל גבוה מסכום דמי הביטוח המתואמים – יהיה העובד זכאי להחזר ההפרש שבין סכום הניכוי בפועל, לבין דמי הביטוח המתואמים.
-- (1) "If the amount deducted from the insured person's total monthly income by all his employers (in
-- this section, the actual deduction) is lower than the amount all his employers would have had to
-- deduct from his total monthly income had it been paid by one employer (in this section, coordinated
-- contributions), the employee is liable to pay the difference ..."; (2) "if the actual deduction is
-- higher ..., the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference."
-- The coordinated contributions are (c) applied to the total monthly income as one employer's wage,
-- with (c)(2) (fork F14): the caller gives that month, with column D amounts on the total.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d), "הניכוי בפועל" (source line 3664)
GIVEN `the amounts each employer deducted` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(d) — "the actual deduction", of` `the amounts each employer deducted` MEANS
    sum `the amounts each employer deducted`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d), "דמי ביטוח מתואמים" (source line 3664)
GIVEN `the month as if paid by one employer` IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month as if paid by one employer` MEANS
    `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` `the month as if paid by one employer`

-- Version 0.3.0: at a reading of Schedule J; at the printed totals, the argument is the column D
-- amount on the total monthly income, for the branches in which a deduction is made, together.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d) (source line 3664); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN `the month as if paid by one employer` IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d) (source line 3664); the switch above
GIVEN `the month as if paid by one employer` IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` `section 342(c) — the reading of Schedule J this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d) (source lines 3663-3665)
GIVEN `the amounts each employer deducted`   IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the month as if paid by one employer` IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
GIVETH A `The outcome of section 342(d)`
`s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` `the amounts each employer deducted` `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month as if paid by one employer` MEANS
    `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` `the amounts each employer deducted` `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month as if paid by one employer`
        `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d) (source lines 3663-3665); the switch above
GIVEN `the amounts each employer deducted`   IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the month as if paid by one employer` IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      `at the totals`                        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The outcome of section 342(d)`
`s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` `the amounts each employer deducted` `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` `the amounts each employer deducted` `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month as if paid by one employer`
        `, reading Schedule J as` `section 342(c) — the reading of Schedule J this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d) (source lines 3663-3665); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN `the amounts each employer deducted`   IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the month as if paid by one employer` IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      r                                      IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `at the totals`                        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The outcome of section 342(d)`
`s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` `the amounts each employer deducted` `and the month as if paid by one employer` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    BRANCH IF count `the amounts each employer deducted` LESS THAN 2
              THEN `section 342(d) does not apply: the insured person works for one employer`
           IF `the actual deduction` LESS THAN `the coordinated contributions`
              THEN `the employee pays the difference` (`the coordinated contributions` MINUS `the actual deduction`)
           IF `the actual deduction` GREATER THAN `the coordinated contributions`
              THEN `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference` (`the actual deduction` MINUS `the coordinated contributions`)
           OTHERWISE `neither paragraph: the actual deduction equals the coordinated contributions`
    WHERE
        `the actual deduction` MEANS `s 342(d) — "the actual deduction", of` `the amounts each employer deducted`
        `the coordinated contributions` MEANS `s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` `the month as if paid by one employer` `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

§§ `342(e) — the Minister's powers`

-- (e)(1)-(4) are powers to make rules: an employee's duty to report another employer, the payment or
-- refund of the (d) difference, the deduction at the full rate where there is another employer, and
-- the Institute's approval of other rates. They decide nothing themselves; the regulations made under
-- them are not in the sources. Carried here as quoted text (above, with (c)) and as the refusal (c)
-- reaches. (e)(3) and (e)(4) say "column E of Schedule J" where the deduction is column D (fork F22;
-- nii-il05-tests-expected-red.l4).

§§ `342(e1) — a member of a renewed kibbutz`

-- src:3672 | (ה1) חבר קיבוץ מתחדש שמתקיים בו האמור בסעיף 3א(א), ונוסף על כך הוא עובד כאמור בסעיף 3א(ב), יחולו על הקיבוץ המתחדש הוראות לפי סעיף קטן (ה)(3), בשינויים המחויבים, והקיבוץ המתחדש ישלם בעד החבר דמי ביטוח בסכום השווה להפרש שבין דמי הביטוח המתואמים ובין הסכום הכולל של דמי הביטוח שנוכו בעד שכרו של החבר המשתלם בידי מעסיקו האחר בעד אותו חודש.
-- "A member of a renewed kibbutz who meets s 3A(a), and who in addition works as stated in s 3A(b): the
-- provisions under (e)(3) apply to the renewed kibbutz, with the necessary changes, and the renewed
-- kibbutz pays for the member contributions equal to the difference between the coordinated
-- contributions and the total contributions deducted for the member's wage paid by his other employer
-- for that month." s 3A is not in this row: whether it is met is an input. Where it is not, (e1) puts
-- nothing on the kibbutz. Where the other employer deducted more than the coordinated contributions,
-- (e1) says nothing of the excess: declined (fork F15).
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e1) (source line 3672)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 342(e1) does not say what follows when the other employer deducted more than the coordinated contributions` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 342(e1) does not say what follows when the other employer deducted more than the coordinated contributions"

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e1) (source line 3672); s 3A (not in this row)
GIVEN k IS A `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` k MEANS
    `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` k `, reading Schedule J as` `the items govern` `, column D at the printed totals being` 0

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e1) (source line 3672); the switch above
GIVEN k              IS A `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` k `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` k `, reading Schedule J as` `section 342(c) — the reading of Schedule J this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e1) (source line 3672); s 3A (not in this row); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN k              IS A `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `at the totals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(e1) — the contributions the renewed kibbutz pays for the member, for` k `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (k's `meets section 3A(a)` AND k's `works as stated in section 3A(b)`)
              THEN 0
           IF `the deducted amount` GREATER THAN `the coordinated contributions`
              THEN `section 342(e1) does not say what follows when the other employer deducted more than the coordinated contributions`
           OTHERWISE `the coordinated contributions` MINUS `the deducted amount`
    WHERE
        `the deducted amount` MEANS k's `contributions deducted for the member's wage by the other employer for the month`
        `the coordinated contributions` MEANS `s 342(d) — "coordinated contributions", for` (k's `the member's month, as if paid by one employer`) `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

§§ `Version 0.4.0: s 342(c), (d) and (e1) on the income s 348(a) takes into account`

-- src:3763 | (א) לענין דמי ביטוח המשתלמים לפי הוראה מהוראות סעיף 335 לא יבוא בחשבון סכום ההכנסה של המבוטח העולה על הסכום המרבי המתקבל לפי האמור בלוח י״א.
-- 05-RC2 (BACKLOG IL-17, 2026-10-08; the independent tester's root cause 2). s 342(c)(1) deducts
-- "percentages of the income on which the contributions are payable" (source line 3661), and s
-- 348(a): "for contributions payable under any provision of s 335, the amount of the insured
-- person's income exceeding the maximum amount obtained under Schedule K shall not be taken into
-- account". The rules above take column D as amounts the caller has computed, so they deduct on
-- whatever income the caller used: column D computed on a wage of 60,000 in 2026 gives 2,522.3811 at
-- the items, where on the 51,910 s 348(a) takes into account it is 2,144.5781. They are kept,
-- answering as before, and their column D amounts must be on the income s 348(a) takes into account.
-- The rules below take the wage instead, and column D as Schedule J gives it, a function of an
-- income: by branch (the items) and for the deduction branches together (the printed totals), row
-- IL-04's `the column D deduction under` on an income, which this row cannot import (NOTES.md section
-- 8). They apply column D to the wage as s 348(a) takes it into account: the wage, or the Schedule K
-- item 1 maximum for a month if the wage is above it. The month's own column D amounts are not read.
-- Fork F25: s 348(b)'s minimum is not applied here. With several employers, whether it applies to
-- each employer's wage or to the total is fork F17, which is not modelled; a caller who applies it
-- gives the minimum as the wage.
@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1) (source line 3661); s 348(a) (source line 3763); Schedule K item 1, maximum, for a month (source line 4758)
GIVEN `the wage` IS A NUMBER
      m          IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      f          IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c)(1) with s 348(a) — the income the deduction is taken on, from a wage of` `the wage` `, for` m `, under` f MEANS
    IF   f's `tax year` EQUALS m's `tax year`
    THEN `s 348(a) — the income taken into account, of` `the wage` `, with the maximum at` (`Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a month, under` f)
    ELSE `the figures given are for another tax year than the case`

-- The month, with column D by branch on that income in place of the amounts it carried.
GIVEN m             IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
      `the amounts` IS A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
GIVETH AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
`s 342(c) — the same month as` m `, with the column D amounts` `the amounts` MEANS
    `An employee's month under section 342(c)` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS m's `tax year`
        `month`                                                               IS m's `month`
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS m's `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`
        `the column D amounts on the wage`                                    IS `the amounts`
        `senior citizen pension`                                              IS m's `senior citizen pension`
        `the insured person`                                                  IS m's `the insured person`
        `date of birth`                                                       IS m's `date of birth`
        `a police officer or a prison officer`                                IS m's `a police officer or a prison officer`
        `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)` IS m's `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(1)-(2) (source lines 3661-3662); s 348(a) (source line 3763); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN `the wage`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc the wage the employer pays for the month, before s 348(a)
      m                            IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`  @desc the month; its column D amounts are not read
      f                            IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`  @desc the figures for the month's tax year, for the Schedule K maximum
      r                            IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      `column D by branch`         IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`  @desc Schedule J column D on an income, branch by branch (row IL-04's column D deduction at the items, per branch)
      `column D at the totals`     IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER  @desc Schedule J column D on an income at the printed totals, for the branches in which the employer deducts together (row IL-04's column D deduction at the printed totals)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from a wage of` `the wage` `, for` m `, under` f `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D by branch on an income being` `column D by branch` `, column D at the printed totals on an income being` `column D at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`s 342(c) — the same month as` m `, with the column D amounts` (`column D by branch` `the income`))
        `, reading Schedule J as` r `, column D at the printed totals being` (`column D at the totals` `the income`)
    WHERE
        `the income` MEANS `s 342(c)(1) with s 348(a) — the income the deduction is taken on, from a wage of` `the wage` `, for` m `, under` f

-- At the reading the switch names, with the Schedule K figures for the month's tax year (2026 as the
